WEBVTT

00:31:24.246 --> 00:31:31.038
You know, what it indicates is clearly
that what we come up with when we ask

00:31:31.038 --> 00:31:34.954
ourselves a question is we are
sampling from our mind.

00:31:34.954 --> 00:31:38.038
We are not extracting the
answers from our mind.

00:31:38.246 --> 00:31:40.496
We are sampling an answer from our mind.

00:31:40.663 --> 00:31:44.788
And there are many different ways
that that sample could come out.

00:31:44.954 --> 00:31:50.496
And sampling twice, especially if you will
make them independent sampling twice

00:31:50.496 --> 00:31:52.621
is going to be better than sampling once.

00:31:54.329 --> 00:31:56.663
This is this is one of the most practical,

00:31:57.538 --> 00:32:02.788
unexpected decision making and judgment
perspectives that I've come across in